<figure class="agent-diagram" aria-labelledby="agent-diagram-caption">
  <div class="diagram-kicker">THE PROBLEM SPACE</div>
  <div class="diagram-flow">
    <div class="diagram-node diagram-node--request">
      <span class="diagram-node__index">01</span>
      <strong>REQUEST</strong>
      <small>user intent</small>
    </div>
    <span class="diagram-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
    <div class="diagram-node diagram-node--agent">
      <span class="diagram-node__index">02</span>
      <strong>LLM AGENT</strong>
      <small>decide to act</small>
    </div>
    <span class="diagram-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
    <div class="diagram-node diagram-node--tool">
      <span class="diagram-node__index">03</span>
      <strong>TOOL</strong>
      <small>retrieve · execute</small>
    </div>
    <span class="diagram-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
    <div class="diagram-node diagram-node--response">
      <span class="diagram-node__index">04</span>
      <strong>RESPONSE</strong>
      <small>belief · output</small>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="diagram-notes" aria-hidden="true">
    <span><i></i> tool admission</span>
    <span><i></i> retrieved context</span>
    <span><i></i> safety behaviour</span>
  </div>
  <figcaption id="agent-diagram-caption">
    Safety is not only a property of the final answer. It can change at the points where an agent decides, retrieves, and acts.
  </figcaption>
